    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="15.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Ine">Ine</ref> 15.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="15.1" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="96" ed="#liebermann"/>Se að sceal bion<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_15-1.lnote.oe.4"/> healf be huslgengum.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="15.1" corresp="#wit-bu"><pb n="96" ed="#liebermann"/>Se að sceal byon healf be huslgengum.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="15.1" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="96" ed="#liebermann"/>Se að sceal beon healf be huslgengum.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="15.1" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="97" ed="#liebermann"/>Se að sceal beon [half<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_15-1.lnote.oe.1"/>] be huslgengu<hi rend="italic">m</hi>.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="15.1" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="97" ed="#liebermann"/>Et debet esse medietas (iurantium<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Ine_15-1.lnote.oe.6"/>) per hulsgengas<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Ine_15-1.lnote.oe.7"/> (id est duodecimhyndos).</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="40" ed="#attenborough"/>Se að sceal bion healf be huslgengum.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="14.3" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="380" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Se að sceal bion healf be huslgengum.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="97" ed="#liebermann"/>Der Eid soll halb [so stark<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_15-1.lnote.de.1"/>] sein bei Abendmahlsgängern.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_15-1.lnote.de.2"/></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">The oath is to be half [as strong] in the case of communicants.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="41" ed="#attenborough"/>An oath equal in value to half the amount shall be sufficient in the case of communicants<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Ine_15-1.attnote.n.1"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="401" ed="#whitelock"/>With communicants, the oath shall be [only] half as much.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="381" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>The oath shall be half for a communicant.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="381"><label>same term (huslgenga)</label> <ref target="clause:Wi_23-a">Wi 23</ref> <quote>The term huslgenga also appears in §19, as well as in Wihtred §18 [L23], which suggests the existence in Kent of legal privileges [...] comparable</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="381"><label>same term (huslgenga)</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_19">Ine 19</ref> <quote>The term huslgenga also appears in §19, as well as in Wihtred §18 [L23], which suggests the existence in Kent of legal privileges [...] comparable</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="383"><label>see</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_19">Ine 19</ref> <quote>See Ine §14.3.</quote></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_15-1.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">97</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">im</hi> 16. <hi rend="italic">Jh. eingefügt</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">inserted in the 16th cent.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_15-1.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">97</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_15-1.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">97</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so Lond;</hi> -gonges <hi rend="italic">übrige</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">thus Lond; -gonges the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_15-1.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">96</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">beon <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">beon Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_15-1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">70</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Die Zahl der Eideshufen, d. h. der sie vertretenden Schwörer</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The number of oath-hides, i.e. of the swearers representing them</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_15-1.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">70</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> abendmahlsfähig. Der Plural beweist, dass auch die Helfer Kommunikanten sein müssen. Q’s falsche Deutung entstand wohl, weil er <hi rend="italic">u.</hi> 19 von einem Abendmahlsgänger dieses Standes las</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> abendmahlsfähig. The plural proves that the helpers too must be communicants. Q’s wrong interpretation probably arose because he read <hi rend="italic">below</hi> 19 of a communicant of this rank</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Ine_15-1.attnote.n.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">185</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. cap. 19 below, where the oath of a communicant appears to be of greater value than that of a non-communicant. For the privileged position of communicants see Wiht. cap. 23.</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
